{
  "repo": "vedprakash-m/tenet-copilot",
  "number": 15,
  "title": "Integrated preview: merge open PRs, disable undo, keep __proto__ keys, cache admission",
  "body": "Integrated **preview** build. It is not qualified and must not be called a release.\n\n## What this branch does\n- Merges open PRs #7, #8, #9, #11, #12, #13 and #14. #10's save is not included.\n- **Disables undo.** `undo` and `decide undo-confirm` exit 2 with `capability-missing`, because undo can overwrite human work. The skill tells the agent to send the user to Git. Tests: `undo-disabled.test.ts` and the UAT undo section. Existing undo tests keep running through a test-only seam.\n- **Keeps the record key `__proto__`.** Persisted state maps use `ownRecord` in place of `z.record`, and the verdict's hash map is built on a null-prototype object (`currentTestHashes`). Before this, a changed support file named `__proto__` could still be reported as `checked-local`. Test: `own-record-keys.test.ts`.\n- **Caches store admission** by file identity and makes `publishState` read state once. This fixes the timing regression from #14: long-history warm p95 went from 904 ms back to 365 ms.\n- **Duplicate-key parser:** whitespace before a colon is now handled with a sticky regex. Test: `unique-record.test.ts`.\n- **README** lists the open safety defects. **CHANGELOG** has an entry dated 2026-11-08.\n\n## CI on `d0f3aa3`\n- `untrusted` passes on ubuntu, macOS and windows-portability. macOS passed on rerun after the known nested-watch canary flake.\n- `system-budgets` **fails NFR-01** (target: warm p95 ≤ 300 ms):\n\n  | Fixture | Warm p95 | Result |\n  |---|---:|---|\n  | small | 260 ms | pass |\n  | large | 328 ms | fail |\n  | long-history | 365 ms | fail |\n\n  Large and long-history already missed the target before the merge (316 ms and 347 ms). What's left is bundle compile, Git spawns and parsing, and reducing those is a design change.\n\n## Known open, not fixed (disclosed in README)\n- Consent applies to more than was shown: dirty-file answers, and a Git hook ran without consent.\n- Recovery removes matching files and does not always report it.\n- Nothing has been observed on the real host (VS Code with Copilot).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
